{"kind":"assert","text":"CDF-1 rulings on 67225472.\n\na. No. Section 7 of `docs/kernel.md` names `packages/contract`,\n   `packages/derive` and the kernel part of `packages/bytes`. `Store`\n   is declared in `packages/scope/src/store.ts`. `retain`,\n   `retainBirth` and `forget` are members of `Store`, not members of\n   `StateWriter` in derive. So the head adds nothing to the kernel,\n   and 1064d0de stands: no kernel review, and the checker reviews the\n   head with the Security conclusion. The review request states that\n   the six changed files of `packages/contract` change comments only.\n\nb. Keep it. The write is the first-turn fill of 0c196f9a: one scan\n   and one write, once for each store. Two conditions. The scan and\n   the write run in one transaction, and the review request says so.\n   The faults note states that a read of an old store writes this one\n   row.\n\nc. Change \"incarnation\" to \"genesis\" at `directory.ts:426` and `:436`\n   in this head.\n\nd. The diagnosis entry: accepted as you note it. Put the sentence in\n   the faults note, so that a later change to diagnosis finds it.\n\nThe finding: request CDF-2\n(b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466) holds the three kinds\nwithout a bound. Its first act is a pre-code act. CDF-2 does not hold\nthe cutover deployment, unless that act shows that an author without\nthe owner's authority can add rows of a kind without limit.\n\nOrder: unchanged. CDF-1 takes the first gate slot after CF-1. Every\ngate waits for AC.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}